# ============================================================================
# SUPABASE SETUP (one-time, ~3 minutes)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. Go to https://supabase.com -> "New project". Give it a name + a strong
#     database password. Wait ~30 seconds for the project to provision.
#  2. In the project sidebar open: Project Settings -> API.
#  3. Copy "Project URL" into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL below.
#  4. Copy the "anon public" key into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below.
#     (Do NOT use the service_role key here — it bypasses RLS.)
#  5. Open SQL Editor -> New query, paste the contents of
#       supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql
#     and click Run. This creates the profiles + tutor_profiles +
#     student_profiles tables and the signup trigger.
#  6. Copy this file to .env.local in the project root and fill in the values.
#  7. Restart `npm run dev` so Next.js picks up the new env vars.
# ============================================================================
#
# AUTH EMAIL (Resend SMTP) — configured in the Supabase dashboard, NOT here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Supabase sends auth emails (signup confirmation), so there is NO Resend key
#  in this file. The built-in Supabase sender is capped at ~2 emails/hour with
#  poor deliverability; route through Resend instead:
#   1. Create a Resend account -> API Keys -> create a key (re_...).
#   2. Supabase -> Project Settings -> Authentication -> SMTP Settings ->
#        Host smtp.resend.com, Port 465 (or 587), Username resend,
#        Password = your re_... key, Sender name TutorMatch,
#        Sender email onboarding@resend.dev (until a domain is verified).
#   3. Supabase -> Authentication -> Emails -> Confirm signup -> paste
#        supabase/email-templates/confirm-signup.html.
#   4. Supabase -> Authentication -> Rate Limits -> raise emails/hour above 2.
#   5. Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration -> set Site URL.
#  TEST MODE: onboarding@resend.dev only delivers to your own Resend account
#  email. To send to anyone, verify a domain in Resend (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) and
#  switch the Sender email to e.g. noreply@yourdomain.com. See README "Configure
#  auth email (Resend SMTP)".
# ============================================================================

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY
